Package: sikdr
Type: Package
Title: Single-Index Kernel Density Regression
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jiayang", "Xu", email = "12313323@mail.sustech.edu.cn", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Yusen", "Jia", role = "aut"),
    person("Yangzhou", "Chen", role = "aut"),
    person("Xin", "Chen", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimation and inference for the single-index model with an error
    independent of the predictors. At each candidate direction the link is refitted
    by a protected leave-one-out kernel smoother and the direction is scored by the
    leave-one-out kernel log-likelihood of the residuals, so skewed or multimodal
    errors inform the direction. Bandwidths are ranked by the trace of a case-weight
    covariance estimate, confidence sets invert a test that is exact under Gaussian
    predictors, and distance-correlation screening extends the method to more
    predictors than observations. Method: Xu, Jia, Chen and Chen (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2611.22384>.
